    "description": "## Objective\n\nLoad the client's exported rates and link data into the sandbox as labeled sample records so the demo shows real partners, operators, deals, and markets.\n\n## Implementation Requirements\n\n* Transform the rates export (143 rows) into Deal records: derive Operator from the Brand column, map Geo to WT_Market values, split rows covering two verticals into two Deals\n* Exclude and log rows with formula errors or legend/junk content\n* Load order: Operators, Partners, Deals, then \\~10 tracking links as Deal-Rep Assignment records with Link Slug populated\n* Prefix every loaded record name with SAMPLE — for one-step purge later\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n* Deals list view shows the loaded partners/brands/markets/rates\n* Loaded row count + logged exclusions = source row count\n* Every loaded record identifiable by the SAMPLE prefix\n\n## Testing Notes\n\nReconciliation count check.\n\n## Out of Scope\n\nProduction data migration (BUILD-07).\n\n## Additional Notes\n\n* The rates file is Digital-side data and is explicitly not the production upload — the Agency-side file will follow. Deal structure is the same on both sides.\n* Keep the transform script/mapping — it becomes the starting point for BUILD-07.\n\n---\n\nEstimate: M · \\~6h · Dependencies: POC-03 to POC-10 · Ticket POC-11 (approved 2026-07-04)",
